  "all_ingredients_flat": "red lentils, 'kala chana besan', small onion, red pepper, green pepper, flaxseed meal, sesame seeds, ginger, garlic cloves, salt, red chili powder, coriander cumin powder, turmeric powder, black pepper powder, cilantro, onion powder",
  "instructions": "Steps for 12-15 Tikkis\n* Cook 1 cup whole red lentils with 1:1 water in Instant Pot for 12 minutes. Let it cool down.\n* Chop 1 small onion, 1/2 red pepper, 1/2 green pepper. Saut\u00e9 them until onion is translucent. Add grated ginger & 3-4 garlic cloves. Continue to saut\u00e9 for 1-2 minutes. Let this mixture cool down.\n* Mix together cooked lentils & saut\u00e9ed veggies in a food processor. Add 1 tbsp flaxseed meal, 1 tbsp sesame seeds, salt as per taste, 1/2 to 1 tsp red chili powder (to taste), 1 tsp coriander cumin powder, 1/2 tsp turmeric powder, 1/4 tsp black pepper powder, 1 cup chopped cilantro, 1 tsp onion powder and 4 tbsp 'kala chana besan'. Mix until combined (not like paste).\n* Air fry at 350F for 10 minutes. Flip and air fry for another 5 minutes until golden brown. Or bake at 350F for 12 minutes; flip and bake for another 10 minutes. Serve with cilantro chutney!",
  "cooking_methods": [
    "boil",
    "saute",
    "air-fry",
    "bake"
  ],
  "serving_suggestion": "Serve with cilantro chutney!",
  "notes": "Yields 12-15 Tikkis.",
